    <node id="Head and Neck Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Head and Neck Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Head and Neck Cancer encompasses cancers that occur in the head and neck region and can impact associated structures and functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Head and neck cancer includes a variety of cancers that develop in the head and neck regions, one of which is mouth cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Head and neck cancer includes various types of cancers that arise in the head and neck region, affecting structures like the throat, mouth, and sinuses.&lt;SEP&gt;Head and neck cancer is a group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area of the body, including mouth cancer and others.&lt;SEP&gt;Head and neck cancer refers to a group of cancers affecting the head and neck region, impacting various structures like the mouth, throat, and nose.&lt;SEP&gt;Head and neck cancer refers to a group of cancers that occur in the head and neck region, impacting various functions and requiring specific medical attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Head and neck cancers are a group of cancer types that arise in the head or neck area, and treatment is based on the tumor location.&lt;SEP&gt;Head and neck cancers can also arise from HPV infections and include cancers of the throat, esophagus, and other areas in the head and neck region.&lt;SEP&gt;Head and neck cancers encompass a group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Squamous Cell Carcinoma (SCC)">
      <data key="d0">Squamous Cell Carcinoma (SCC)</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Squamous Cell Carcinoma is the most common type of mouth cancer, originating in the squamous cells lining the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;Squamous Cell Carcinoma is the most common type of nasopharyngeal cancer, forming in the thin, flat cells of the mucous membranes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
