    <node id="Tumor">
      <data key="d0">Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A tumor in the context of primary CNS lymphoma refers to an abnormal growth of lymphocytes that exerts pressure on surrounding brain tissue, leading to symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;A tumor is an abnormal growth of cells that can be benign or malignant, commonly associated with cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A tumor is an abnormal mass of tissue resulting from excessive cell division, which can be benign or malignant, and may develop in various locations of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A tumor is an abnormal mass of tissue that can be benign or malignant, often associated with cancer and requiring medical evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;A tumor is an abnormal mass of tissue that can be benign or malignant, with gliomas being a specific type that affects the brain.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumors are abnormal masses of tissue that can be benign or malignant, with characteristics affecting their resectability and prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
