    <node id="Pancreatic Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Pancreatic Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that affects the pancreas, making it challenging to diagnose and treat; expertise is focused on improving treatment options.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the tissues of the pancreas and is known for being complex and challenging to diagnose and treat.&lt;SEP&gt;Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that forms in the tissues of the pancreas and is characterized by various stages indicating how far the disease has progressed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pancreas">
      <data key="d0">Pancreas</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The pancreas is a vital organ that produces digestive enzymes and hormones, located behind the stomach and crucial for metabolic functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas produces digestive enzymes and hormones, playing a crucial role in digestion and blood sugar regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter 1: Introduction">
      <data key="d0">Chapter 1: Introduction</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter 1 provides an introduction to the topics of leukemia and cancer treatment, setting the stage for more detailed discussions in subsequent chapters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
