      <data key="d0">Genetic and Biomarker Mutation Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic and biomarker mutation testing is a critical aspect of diagnosing and treating ALL, helping to tailor therapies to individual patient needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Patient Advocacy Groups">
      <data key="d0">Patient Advocacy Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Patient advocacy groups are organizations that provide support and resources to patients navigating their healthcare journeys, particularly in cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Patient advocacy groups support families and individuals dealing with cancer by providing resources, information, and a community.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Pancreatic adenocarcinoma is a common type of pancreatic cancer that is of significant focus in discussing treatment strategies and challenges.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lifestyle Factors">
      <data key="d0">Lifestyle Factors</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Lifestyle factors include personal habits such as diet, exercise, and smoking that can influence the risk of prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Lifestyle factors refer to habits and practices such as diet, exercise, and smoking, which can influence cancer risk and general health.&lt;SEP&gt;Lifestyle factors such as smoking, heavy alcohol use, and a less healthy diet are known to increase the risk of developing pancreatic cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hereditary Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Hereditary Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Hereditary conditions such as HBOC, Peutz-Jeghers syndrome, Lynch syndrome, and others are linked to an increased risk of pancreatic cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Hereditary conditions such as HBOC, Peutz-Jeghers syndrome, and Lynch syndrome increase the risk of pancreatic cancer through genetic predisposition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 0 Pancreatic Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage 0 Pancreatic Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 0 pancreatic cancer refers to cancer only present in the innermost layer of the duct wall and is at an initial stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 0 pancreatic cancer refers to the earliest stage where the cancer is localized to the innermost layer of the duct wall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1 Pancreatic Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1 Pancreatic Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1 pancreatic cancer consists of a tumor that is 4 centimeters or smaller and has not spread outside the pancreas.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1 pancreatic cancer consists of a tumor that is 4 centimeters or smaller and has not yet spread beyond the pancreas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 2 Pancreatic Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage 2 Pancreatic Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 2 pancreatic cancer consists of tumors larger than 4 centimeters or cancer spread to nearby lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 2 pancreatic cancer involves a larger tumor or cancer that has spread to up to three nearby lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 3 Pancreatic Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage 3 Pancreatic Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 3 pancreatic cancer has grown through the pancreas or has spread to four or more lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 3 pancreatic cancer indicates that the cancer has invaded nearby major arteries or has spread to four or more lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 4 Pancreatic Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage 4 Pancreatic Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 4 pancreatic cancer is characterized by metastasis, where the cancer has spread to distant organs like the liver or lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 4 pancreatic cancer is metastatic, meaning it has spread to distant sites such as the liver or lungs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Heavy Alcohol Use">
      <data key="d0">Heavy Alcohol Use</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Heavy alcohol use is another lifestyle factor that increases the likelihood of developing pancreatic cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unhealthy Diet">
      <data key="d0">Unhealthy Diet</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">An unhealthy diet is a lifestyle factor that contributes to the risk of pancreatic cancer along with other cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diabetes">
      <data key="d0">Diabetes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Diabetes is a health condition that has been associated with an increased risk of developing pancreatic cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chronic Inflammation of the Pancreas">
      <data key="d0">Chronic Inflammation of the Pancreas</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Chronic inflammation of the pancreas is a significant health condition that raises the risk of pancreatic cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HBOC">
      <data key="d0">HBOC</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Hereditary breast-ovarian cancer syndrome (HBOC) is a genetic condition associated with increased risks of certain cancers, including pancreatic cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Peutz-Jeghers Syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Peutz-Jeghers Syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Peutz-Jeghers syndrome is a genetic disorder that raises the risk of developing various types of cancer, including pancreatic cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Familial Malignant Melanoma Syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Familial Malignant Melanoma Syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Familial malignant melanoma syndrome raises the risk for multiple cancers, such as melanoma and pancreatic cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hereditary Pancreatitis">
      <data key="d0">Hereditary Pancreatitis</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Hereditary pancreatitis is a genetic condition that can lead to an increased risk of pancreatic cancer due to chronic inflammation of the pancreas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diagnostic Radiologist">
      <data key="d0">Diagnostic Radiologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A diagnostic radiologist interprets imaging examinations that help in the diagnosis of various cancers, including bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A diagnostic radiologist interprets imaging tests to assist in cancer diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;A diagnostic radiologist is a medical professional who specializes in interpreting medical imaging to diagnose conditions such as cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gastroenterologist">
      <data key="d0">Gastroenterologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A gastroenterologist is a specialist in diagnosing and treating digestive system disorders, including cancers of the gastrointestinal tract.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Geriatrician">
      <data key="d0">Geriatrician</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A geriatrician is a doctor who specializes in the healthcare of older adults and the diseases that affect them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Palliative Care Provider">
      <data key="d0">Palliative Care Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A palliative care provider focuses on improving the quality of life for patients by managing symptoms, pain, and stress related to serious illnesses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mental Health Provider">
      <data key="d0">Mental Health Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A mental health provider assists patients in coping with the emotional impacts of cancer diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Care Plan">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Care Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A cancer care plan is a detailed strategy involving diagnosis, treatment options, and management of a patient’s cancer symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Symptoms of Pancreatic Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Symptoms of Pancreatic Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The symptoms of pancreatic cancer can include jaundice, weight loss, and abnormal blood tests, often making diagnosis challenging as these signs can resemble other health issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Multidisciplinary Consult">
      <data key="d0">Multidisciplinary Consult</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A multidisciplinary consult is a meeting of various healthcare providers to discuss a patient's condition and the most effective approach to treatment in complex cases like cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biopsies">
      <data key="d0">Biopsies</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Biopsies are medical procedures involving the extraction of tissue samples for laboratory examination, often used for cancer diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Biopsies are medical procedures that involve extracting tissue to be examined for cancer cells and other abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Biopsies involve taking a sample of tissue to examine for cancer cells, serving as a definitive method to diagnose cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Biopsies involve the extraction of tissue samples for testing, providing critical information on the presence of cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Screening">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Screening</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer screening involves tests and exams to detect cancer before symptoms appear, aiming for early diagnosis and better outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer screening, including colonoscopy, is crucial for early detection of polyps and cancers, leading to better outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate">
      <data key="d0">Prostate</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The Prostate is a gland in the male reproductive system that can be affected by prostate cancer, playing a critical role in men's health.&lt;SEP&gt;The prostate is a gland in the male reproductive system that produces seminal fluid and is crucial for reproductive health.&lt;SEP&gt;The prostate is a gland situated near the bladder and urethra that is often removed during radical cystectomy if affected by cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The prostate is a small gland located below the bladder in men, playing a key role in the reproductive system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSA">
      <data key="d0">PSA</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">PSA (Prostate-specific antigen) is a protein produced by the prostate gland, which can indicate prostate issues, including cancer, if present in high levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate-specific antigen (PSA) is a protein produced by the prostate gland that helps in the evaluation of prostate health and cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Semen">
      <data key="d0">Semen</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Semen is a fluid containing sperm and fluids from the prostate and seminal vesicles, essential for reproduction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Seminal Vesicles">
      <data key="d0">Seminal Vesicles</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Seminal vesicles are glands that produce a significant portion of the fluid that becomes semen, located above the prostate and behind the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;The seminal vesicles are two glands that produce and store a significant part of the fluid component of semen, located above the prostate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Black Males">
      <data key="d0">Black Males</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Black males are statistically more likely to develop prostate cancer, often at a younger age and with increased severity compared to other demographics.&lt;SEP&gt;Black males in the United States have a higher prevalence of prostate cancer compared to other racial groups, facing earlier onset and more aggressive forms of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Early-Stage Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Early-Stage Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Early-stage prostate cancer has not spread beyond the prostate and is generally slow-growing and highly treatable.&lt;SEP&gt;Early-stage prostate cancer is highly treatable and often curable, and it typically has not spread outside the prostate gland.&lt;SEP&gt;Early-stage prostate cancer refers to cancer that has not spread outside of the prostate and typically grows slowly, allowing for various treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Advanced-Stage Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Advanced-Stage Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Advanced-stage prostate cancer indicates that cancer has spread beyond the prostate to other parts of the body, including lymph nodes and organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced-stage prostate cancer indicates the cancer has metastasized beyond the prostate to other parts of the body, presenting challenges in treatment and management.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced-stage prostate cancer refers to cases where the cancer has spread and is usually associated with a life-long disease that can be managed with treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced-stage prostate cancer refers to the later stages of the disease, typically with significant progression and symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate Gland">
      <data key="d0">Prostate Gland</data>
      <data key="d1">geo</data>
      <data key="d2">The prostate gland is a reproductive organ in males, situated below the bladder and surrounding the urethra, playing a crucial role in semen production.&lt;SEP&gt;The prostate gland is a small gland in men that produces prostate-specific antigen and plays a role in reproductive health.&lt;SEP&gt;The prostate gland is a vital part of the male reproductive system, responsible for producing seminal fluid and a protein known as prostate-specific antigen (PSA).&lt;SEP&gt;The prostate gland is located just below the bladder in the pelvis and plays a vital role in male reproductive health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Erectile Dysfunction">
      <data key="d0">Erectile Dysfunction</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Erectile dysfunction refers to the inability to achieve or maintain an erection, which can be associated with prostate health issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Groin Pain">
