    </node>
    <node id="Screening Tests">
      <data key="d0">Screening Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Screening tests are medical evaluations that may help in the early detection of prostate cancer, especially in high-risk groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening tests are medical examinations aimed at early detection of prostate cancer, particularly for high-risk populations like Black males.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening tests for liver cancer include ultrasound and alpha-fetoprotein tests, both essential for early detection of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Localized Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Localized Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Localized prostate cancer refers to cancer that is confined within the prostate gland and has not spread to other areas of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Localized prostate cancer refers to the early stage of prostate cancer where the disease remains confined within the prostate gland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Metastatic Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Metastatic Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Metastatic prostate cancer is a more advanced form of the disease where cancer cells spread beyond the prostate to lymph nodes and other organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Metastatic prostate cancer is an advanced stage where the cancer has spread beyond the prostate to other parts of the body, such as lymph nodes, bones, or organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Metastatic prostate cancer refers to advanced prostate cancer that has spread beyond the prostate to other parts of the body, requiring specific diagnostic and therapeutic approaches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Active Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Active Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Active Surveillance is a management strategy for low-risk thyroid cancers that involves monitoring rather than immediate treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Active surveillance is a management strategy for early-stage prostate cancer that involves regular tests without immediate treatment unless changes occur.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
