      <data key="d0">PSA Test</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The PSA test is a blood test measuring prostate-specific antigen levels to assess the risk of prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The PSA test is a blood test used to measure prostate-specific antigen levels, often used for detecting prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The PSA test is a blood test used to measure prostate-specific antigen levels, which can indicate the presence of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d0">Digital Rectal Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A digital rectal exam is a medical procedure where a doctor examines the prostate through the rectal wall to check for abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital rectal exam is a medical test where a doctor checks the prostate for abnormalities by inserting a gloved finger into the rectum.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital rectal exam is a procedure where a doctor checks the prostate's size and texture, often used in conjunction with PSA testing to assess prostate health.&lt;SEP&gt;A digital rectal exam is a procedure where a doctor examines the prostate through the rectum, checking for abnormalities such as tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;Digital rectal exam is a physical examination where a doctor feels the prostate through the rectal wall to check for abnormalities such as lumps or hard areas.&lt;SEP&gt;The digital rectal exam is a physical examination technique used in conjunction with PSA testing to assess prostate health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Treatments">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Treatments</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer treatments encompass various medical interventions aimed at eliminating or controlling cancer cells, including surgery, chemotherapy, and immunotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer treatments encompass various medical interventions, including surgery, radiation, chemotherapy, and hormone therapy, tailored to individual cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer treatments for prostate cancer include surgery, radiation therapy, hormone therapy, chemotherapy, and other targeted therapies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate-Specific Antigen (PSA) Test">
      <data key="d0">Prostate-Specific Antigen (PSA) Test</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The PSA test is a blood test used to measure prostate-specific antigen levels, which can indicate the presence of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Hormone Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Hormone Therapy refers to a range of treatments that alter hormone levels, commonly used in the management of prostate and breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone therapy for prostate cancer involves treatments that alter hormone levels, including using LHRH agonists and antagonists, anti-androgens, and corticosteroids.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone therapy involves the use of medication to modify hormone levels, often used in the treatment of prostate cancer to control tumor growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone therapy is a treatment approach used in prostate cancer to block hormones that fuel the growth of cancer cells, particularly in advanced stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone therapy is a treatment that aims to block the body's natural hormones that can promote cancer growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Urine Tests">
      <data key="d0">Urine Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Urine tests are additional diagnostic measures used alongside blood tests to assess prostate health, detecting potential issues through biomarkers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
    </node>
