      <data key="d0">PSMA/PET Imaging</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">PSMA/PET imaging is an advanced type of PET scanning that targets prostate-specific membrane antigen on prostate cancer cells, enhancing detection of prostate cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bone Scan">
      <data key="d0">Bone Scan</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Bone Scan is a diagnostic imaging test that uses a radiotracer to detect areas of bone damage or abnormalities in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A Bone Scan is a diagnostic procedure that detects the presence of cancer that has spread to the bones, providing critical information for patient management.&lt;SEP&gt;A bone scan is a specific imaging test used to observe the health of bones and detect cancer-related issues.&lt;SEP&gt;A bone scan is an imaging test that uses a radioactive tracer to evaluate bone health and detect cancer spread to bones.&lt;SEP&gt;A bone scan is an imaging test that uses a radiotracer to detect bone abnormalities, often linked to cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone scan is a diagnostic procedure used to determine if prostate cancer has spread to the bones, utilizing a radioactive tracer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PSA Level">
      <data key="d0">PSA Level</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">PSA Level refers to the measurement of prostate-specific antigen in the bloodstream, which is used to assess the risk of prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;PSA level refers to the concentration of prostate-specific antigen in the blood, often used as an indicator of prostate health or the presence of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;PSA level refers to the concentration of prostate-specific antigen in the blood, used as a biomarker in evaluating prostate health and potential prostate cancer.</data>
