    <edge source="Pathologist" target="Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">67.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A biopsy is performed to provide tissue samples that a pathologist analyzes to confirm cancer presence.&lt;SEP&gt;Biopsies provide samples that are analyzed by pathologists to confirm cancer diagnoses and determine the subtype of cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathologists analyze biopsy samples to determine the presence of cancerous cells, critical for prostate cancer diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathologists analyze biopsy samples to diagnose the type and extent of ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathologists examine biopsy samples to identify cancer types and grades, essential for the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;The pathologist examines biopsy samples to confirm whether nodules are cancerous and to identify cancer type.</data>
