    <edge source="Lymphatic System" target="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d4">44.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lymphocytes are a critical component of the lymphatic system, helping in immune responses and fighting diseases like Hodgkin lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphocytes are a key component of the lymphatic system, crucial for immune responses against infections.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphocytes are integral components of the lymphatic system, crucial for immune responses and the overall functionality of this system.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphocytes are produced and operated within the lymphatic system, which is fundamental to the immune response against Hodgkin lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;The lymphatic system is integral for lymphocyte circulation and immune response, playing a holistic role in the body's defense mechanisms.</data>
