      <data key="d5">ALL affects the bone marrow's ability to produce healthy blood cells due to overcrowding by immature lymphoblasts.&lt;SEP&gt;ALL originates within the bone marrow where lymphocytes are produced and where the disease manifests.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone marrow is the origin of blood cells that are affected in ALL, playing a significant role in the disease and treatment process.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone marrow is the site of blood cell production that is primarily affected in acute lymphoblastic leukemia, making it critical for diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer origin, blood cell production&lt;SEP&gt;disease impact, blood production&lt;SEP&gt;disease origin, medical context</data>
