      <data key="d7">chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Transvaginal Ultrasound" target="Cancer">
      <data key="d4">13.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Transvaginal ultrasound can assist in examining the cervix and nearby areas in patients with cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Transvaginal ultrasound is often used to assess the cervix and surrounding tissues for signs of cancer in women.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic imaging, reproductive health</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Contrast Agent" target="CT Scan">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Contrast agents are used during CT scans to improve the clarity and detail of images when assessing for ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Contrast agents are used during CT scans to improve the quality and clarity of images, enhancing the detection of ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic enhancement, imaging technique&lt;SEP&gt;imaging enhancement, diagnostic procedure</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRCA1" target="Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d4">25.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Mutations in the BRCA1 gene are known to increase the risk of developing prostate cancer among other cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Mutations in the BRCA1 gene can increase the risk of developing prostate cancer, highlighting genetic factors in disease predisposition.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic mutation, cancer risk&lt;SEP&gt;genetic risk, cancer correlation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRCA1" target="Cancer Risk">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Mutations in the BRCA1 gene are associated with a higher cancer risk, particularly for breast and prostate cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic mutation, cancer association</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRCA2" target="Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d4">25.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Like BRCA1, mutations in BRCA2 are associated with an increased risk of prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Mutations in BRCA2 also contribute to heightened prostate cancer risk, indicating the relevance of genetic factors in male health issues.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic mutation, cancer risk&lt;SEP&gt;genetic risk, cancer correlation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRCA2" target="Cancer Risk">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Mutations in the BRCA2 gene increase the risk for various cancers, including prostate, breast, and ovarian cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic mutation, cancer association</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Genetic Counselor" target="Germline Testing">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A genetic counselor provides guidance on whether one should undergo germline testing based on personal and family health history.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic consultation, testing recommendation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Genetic Counselor" target="Genetic Test">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Genetic counselors play a key role in helping individuals understand and decide about genetic testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic counselors provide support and interpretation for patients undergoing genetic testing for cancer risks.</data>
      <data key="d6">professional support, genetic testing</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Genetic Counselor" target="Healthcare Provider">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Healthcare providers collaborate with genetic counselors to offer comprehensive care and testing options for patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">patient care, professional collaboration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Radiotracer" target="Bone Scan">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A Radiotracer is essential for conducting a Bone Scan as it helps to visualize the areas of the bone being examined.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, imaging technology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Tumor Markers" target="Blood Tests">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood tests can provide essential information regarding tumor markers, indicating the presence of ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic relevance, health monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fertility-Sparing Surgery" target="IVF">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">IVF may be considered a follow-up reproductive option for patients who undergo fertility-sparing surgery.</data>
      <data key="d6">assisted reproduction, post-surgery options</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Fertility-Sparing Surgery" target="In Vitro Fertilization (IVF)">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">IVF may be utilized after fertility-sparing surgery to help women conceive post-cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">reproductive health, cancer recovery</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Microsatellite Instability (MSI)" target="Tumor Mutational Burden (TMB)">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">MSI and TMB are both important factors in assessing tumor characteristics which influence treatment choices.</data>
      <data key="d6">tumor characteristics, treatment guidance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Microsatellite Instability (MSI)" target="Mismatch Repair (MMR)">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Defects in MMR lead to microsatellite instability, which is a biomarker for certain cancers, including ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic factors, cancer biology</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Microsatellite Instability (MSI)" target="Somatic Mutation">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Somatic mutations can lead to microsatellite instability (MSI), which is associated with specific types of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">mutation, cancer</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Microsatellite Instability (MSI)" target="Deficient Mismatch Repair (dMMR)">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Microsatellite instability (MSI) often results from deficient mismatch repair (dMMR), impacting tumor behavior.</data>
      <data key="d6">DNA repair deficiency, cancer progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Initial Surgery" target="Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The initial surgery for ovarian cancer often includes a biopsy to confirm diagnosis and inform treatment plans.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical intervention, diagnostic confirmation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hysterectomy" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hysterectomy is a major surgical procedure often used to treat cervical cancer, impacting a woman's reproductive capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Hysterectomy is performed to treat cervical cancer, often resulting in the removal of the uterus and cervix, affecting reproductive health.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgery, cancer treatment&lt;SEP&gt;surgical treatment, cancer care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hysterectomy" target="Surgical Menopause">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgical menopause results from a hysterectomy when ovaries are also removed, leading to sudden hormonal changes affecting quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical consequence, hormonal changes</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Microscopic Metastases" target="Surgical Staging">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Microscopic metastases can only be identified during surgical staging, which is essential for accurate cancer staging.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, cancer spread</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Microscopic Metastases" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">During surgery, the team checks for microscopic metastases to ensure comprehensive treatment of ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical consideration, cancer spread</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Interval Cytoreductive Surgery (ICS)" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">ICS is a surgical approach taken after chemotherapy to remove residual ovarian cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical procedure, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Interval Cytoreductive Surgery (ICS)" target="Hyperthermic Intraperitoneal Chemotherapy (HIPEC)">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">HIPEC is administered during ICS to enhance treatment efficacy against remaining cancer cells in the abdominal cavity.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical treatment, chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Interval Cytoreductive Surgery (ICS)" target="American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC)">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">AJCC’s staging system helps determine the appropriateness of ICS in the treatment plan for ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The AJCC staging informs the timing and necessity of ICS in treating ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">staging, treatment guidance&lt;SEP&gt;staging, treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Interval Cytoreductive Surgery (ICS)" target="International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics (FIGO)">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">FIGO's staging system is utilized to guide decision-making for ICS in ovarian cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;FIGO’s staging system is utilized to guide the decision-making process for ICS in ovarian cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">staging, treatment guidance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Interval Cytoreductive Surgery (ICS)" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemotherapy may be administered before ICS to shrink the tumor and make surgery more effective.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment sequence, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC)" target="Oropharyngeal Cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The AJCC establishes a staging system for oropharyngeal cancer to help guide treatment based on tumor characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d6">staging system, treatment guidance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC)" target="Tumor, Node, Metastasis (TNM) System">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">AJCC developed the TNM system to standardize the staging of various cancers, including anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical organization, cancer staging</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </edge>
