      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Peritoneal Washing" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Peritoneal washing is a procedure often performed during surgery to test for cancer cells in the abdominal cavity.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical procedure, diagnostic assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Paclitaxel" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">26.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Paclitaxel is a key component of the chemotherapy regimen used to treat ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Paclitaxel is used as part of the chemotherapy regimen for treating ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Paclitaxel, often used alongside carboplatin, is a key drug in chemotherapy for metastatic anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">chemotherapy agents, cancer treatment&lt;SEP&gt;treatment regimen, drug combination</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Paclitaxel" target="Taxanes">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Paclitaxel is a specific type of taxane used as a chemotherapy drug in treating ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">chemotherapy agent, drug class</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Paclitaxel" target="Combination Regimen">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Paclitaxel is often paired with cisplatin in combination regimens to improve efficacy against metastatic cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment synergy, chemotherapy combination</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bevacizumab" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bevacizumab can be added to chemotherapy regimens to enhance treatment effectiveness by inhibiting tumor feeding blood vessel growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Bevacizumab can be prescribed alongside chemotherapy to impede the vascularization of tumors, enhancing overall treatment efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d6">medication, treatment enhancement&lt;SEP&gt;treatment enhancement, cancer therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bevacizumab" target="Platinum-resistant Cancer">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bevacizumab is recommended for treatment options in cases of platinum-resistant ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">recurrence treatment, chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Thinners" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood thinners are prescribed post-surgery to prevent complications such as DVT, especially in cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-operative care, prevention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Surgical Menopause" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Removal of both ovaries during surgery leads to surgical menopause in patients who have not yet entered menopause.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical effect, hormonal change</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Surgical Menopause" target="Vaginal Atrophy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Vaginal atrophy can develop as a consequence of surgical menopause, impacting post-surgical quality of life for women.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-surgical condition, quality of life</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bevacizumab (Avastin)" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bevacizumab may be added to chemotherapy regimens to enhance treatment effectiveness for ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment enhancement, drug addition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bevacizumab (Avastin)" target="Platinum-resistant Cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bevacizumab can be used effectively in treating ovarian cancer that is resistant to platinum-based chemotherapy."}</data>
      <data key="d6">recurrence treatment, drug therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Peripheral Neuropathy" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Peripheral neuropathy is a common side effect associated with the use of certain chemotherapy agents, including those for ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">side effect, treatment impact</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Neoadjuvant Therapy" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Neoadjuvant therapy involves chemotherapy aimed at reducing tumor size before surgical intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;Neoadjuvant therapy often involves chemotherapy given before surgery to shrink tumors in breast cancer cases.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment strategy, pre-surgery&lt;SEP&gt;treatment strategy, pre-surgical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Neoadjuvant Therapy" target="Drug Interactions">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Drug interactions need careful management when administering neoadjuvant therapy to ensure treatment efficacy is not compromised.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment management, drug safety</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Adjuvant Chemotherapy" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Adjuvant chemotherapy is used after surgery to ensure elimination of remaining cancer cells in ovarian cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment strategy, post-surgical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Olaparib" target="Maintenance Therapy">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Olaparib is commonly used as a maintenance therapy for patients with BRCA-mutated ovarian cancer after chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Olaparib is frequently employed as a maintenance therapy for ovarian cancer patients with BRCA mutations to prolong the treatment benefits.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment option, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Olaparib" target="Niraparib">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Niraparib is often regarded as a backup option to Olaparib in cases where patients cannot tolerate or do not respond to Olaparib.&lt;SEP&gt;Niraparib is used as an alternative to Olaparib in maintenance therapy when Olaparib is not an option for the patient.</data>
      <data key="d6">alternative therapy, cancer care&lt;SEP&gt;alternative therapy, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Olaparib" target="Stage 2 Ovarian Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Olaparib is proposed as an effective maintenance therapy for patients diagnosed with stage 2 ovarian cancer."}&lt;SEP&gt;Olaparib may be used in maintenance therapy for patients diagnosed with stage 2 ovarian cancer who are eligible for treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer treatment, maintenance therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Olaparib" target="Platinum-sensitive Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Olaparib can be administered as maintenance therapy after successful treatment in cases of platinum-sensitive cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Olaparib is often utilized as a maintenance therapeutic option for patients whose cancers respond positively to platinum-based treatment."}</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer treatment, maintenance therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
    </edge>
