      <data key="d5">Hysterectomy is often recommended as a treatment for cervical cancer, especially in specific stages of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical treatment, cancer care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cervical cancer" target="cone biopsy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Cone biopsy is used to diagnose the presence of cervical cancer and determine the appropriate treatment plan.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, early detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="hysterectomy" target="cancer stage 1B">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hysterectomy is often the recommended treatment for stage 1B cervical cancer due to the progression of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical procedure, cancer stage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cancer stage 1A" target="modified radical hysterectomy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">For stage 1A cervical cancer, modified radical hysterectomy is a common surgical method for treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment option, cancer stage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="platinum chemotherapy" target="chemoradiation">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Platinum chemotherapy is often used alongside chemoradiation as part of a treatment regimen for cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">combination therapy, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="surgical staging" target="pelvic lymph nodes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgical staging involves the examination of pelvic lymph nodes to assess for cancer spread during surgical procedures.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer assessment, surgical procedure</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="surgical staging" target="para-aortic lymph nodes">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Para-aortic lymph nodes may be assessed during surgical staging to determine the extent of cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer assessment, lymph nodes</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="locally advanced cancer" target="chemo-radiation">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Locally advanced cervical cancer often requires a treatment plan that includes chemoradiation as it is critical for controlling the disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">advanced treatment, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="follow-up visits" target="surveillance">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Follow-up visits are a vital part of the surveillance process to monitor patients for signs of recurrence after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-treatment care, monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LVSI" target="cancer staging">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The presence of LVSI in a biopsy affects the cancer staging and treatment planning for cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">pathological finding, cancer progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Follow-Up Visits" target="Imaging">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging is often performed during follow-up visits to check for signs of cancer recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging studies are typically performed during follow-up visits to monitor for potential recurrence of cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic imaging, patient monitoring&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic testing, patient monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Follow-Up Visits" target="Glioma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Follow-up visits are critical in the ongoing management of gliomas to detect any recurrence after initial treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">monitoring, treatment effectiveness</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging" target="CT Scan">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">CT scans are a type of imaging test frequently used for visualizing cancer spread in the body, particularly beyond the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic imaging, cancer assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging" target="MRI">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">MRI is another imaging technology utilized to visualize detailed structures and detect cancer influences in the urinary tract.</data>
      <data key="d6">imaging techniques, cancer diagnosis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging" target="Cancer Surveillance">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Regular imaging is part of cancer surveillance to ensure there is no recurrence of anal cancer post-treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">monitoring, follow-up care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging" target="Follow-Up Exam">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Follow-Up Exams often incorporate Imaging to check for any signs of cancer recurrence."&lt;&lt;"monitoring, diagnostic evaluation</data>
      <data key="d6">9</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Immunotherapies" target="PD-L1 Testing">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">PD-L1 testing is essential to identify patients who may respond to specific immunotherapy treatments.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment optimization, personalized medicine</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pelvic Exenteration" target="Urinary Diversions">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Urinary diversions may be necessary during pelvic exenteration due to bladder removal or reconfiguration.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical treatment, waste management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stoma" target="Indiana Pouch">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Indiana Pouch requires a stoma for urine to exit the body, creating a necessary connection for this type of urinary diversion.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical connection, urinary diversion</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mediastinal Gray Zone Lymphoma" target="Primary Mediastinal B-cell Lymphoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Mediastinal gray zone lymphoma shares features with primary mediastinal B-cell lymphoma, influencing treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype relationship, treatment consideration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Metastatic Cervical Cancer" target="Clinical Trials">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Clinical trials often evaluate new therapies for metastatic cervical cancer, offering patients alternative treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d6">research, treatment innovation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PD-L1 Biomarker" target="Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The PD-L1 biomarker influences the effectiveness of immune checkpoint inhibitors like Pembrolizumab in treating certain cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">biomarker relevance, treatment decision</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Thyroid Gland">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thyroid cancer originates from the thyroid gland, making it fundamental to the understanding of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer origin, biological connection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Thyroid Nodules">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thyroid nodules can be precursors to thyroid cancer, thus relating them directly in the context of cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer risk factors, abnormal growths</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Radiation Exposure">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Exposure to radiation increases the likelihood of developing thyroid cancer, establishing a direct risk relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation exposure is a significant risk factor for the development of thyroid cancer, demonstrating a clear causal relationship.</data>
      <data key="d6">risk factor, causation&lt;SEP&gt;risk factors</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="NCCN Guidelines for Patients">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The NCCN provides guidelines that help patients understand and manage thyroid cancer, linking medical education to the disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">patient resources, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Cowden Syndrome">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Cowden syndrome enhances the risk for developing thyroid cancer among affected individuals, highlighting the link between syndromes and cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer predisposition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia (MEN)">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">MEN increases the likelihood of thyroid cancer, indicating a significant relationship between endocrine tumors and cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d6">endocrine tumors</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Levoxyl">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Levoxyl is commonly prescribed for managing thyroid hormone levels in patients with thyroid cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Levoxyl is prescribed to maintain hormone balance in patients undergoing treatment for thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormone replacement, cancer treatment&lt;SEP&gt;medication usage, thyroid treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Synthroid">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Synthroid is another medication used similarly to manage hormone levels in thyroid cancer patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Synthroid serves the same purpose as Levoxyl in managing thyroid hormone levels for cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormone replacement, cancer treatment&lt;SEP&gt;medication usage, thyroid treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Thyroid-stimulating Hormone (TSH)">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Maintaining TSH levels is essential in the treatment and management of thyroid cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;TSH levels are critically maintained during thyroid cancer treatment to prevent cancer cell growth.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormonal regulation, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Radioactive Iodine Therapy">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">RAI therapy is specifically designed to target and eliminate thyroid cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer treatment, targeted therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Endocrinologist">
      <data key="d4">23.0</data>
      <data key="d5">An endocrinologist is involved in the team that treats thyroid cancer patients, managing hormone therapies.&lt;SEP&gt;An endocrinologist is part of the treatment team managing patients with thyroid cancer and their hormone needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Endocrinologists are involved in the treatment of patients diagnosed with thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical collaboration, specialized care&lt;SEP&gt;medical specialty, cancer treatment&lt;SEP&gt;medical team, specialized care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery may be utilized to remove thyroid cancerous tissues before further treatments can proceed.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment procedure, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Thyrotropin Alfa (Thyrogen)">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thyrogen is employed to enhance TSH levels in preparation for treatments such as RAI for thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormonal therapy, treatment preparation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Whole-body RAI Scan">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A Whole-body RAI scan is performed post RAI therapy to check for any residual thyroid cancer presence.&lt;SEP&gt;The Whole-body RAI scan is a crucial step post-RAI therapy to monitor for residual thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">monitoring treatment, imaging procedure&lt;SEP&gt;monitoring, post-treatment assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Levothyroxine">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Levothyroxine is essential for patients with thyroid cancer to manage their hormone levels post-surgery or treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormone replacement, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Radioactive Iodine Therapy (RAI)">
      <data key="d4">19.0</data>
      <data key="d5">RAI therapy is often administered after surgical treatment of thyroid cancer to eliminate residual cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;RAI therapy specifically aims to destroy thyroid cancer cells after thyroidectomy or if cancer is recurrent.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-surgery treatment, cancer care&lt;SEP&gt;targeted treatment, cancer therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Calcium and Vitamin D Supplements">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Calcium and Vitamin D supplements may be recommended to prevent bone weakening during thyroid treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">preventative care, treatment support</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Total Thyroidectomy">
      <data key="d4">28.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Total thyroidectomy is a primary surgical treatment option for patients diagnosed with thyroid cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Total thyroidectomy is often performed as a primary treatment for thyroid cancer to remove malignant tissue and decrease recurrence risk."|&lt;SEP&gt;Total thyroidectomy is often performed as a treatment for thyroid cancer, aiming to remove the cancerous tissue."|</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical treatment, cancer care&lt;SEP&gt;surgical treatment, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;surgical treatment, disease management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Lobectomy">
      <data key="d4">24.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lobectomy can be considered for certain low-risk thyroid cancer cases, providing an alternative to total thyroidectomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Lobectomy is a surgical option for thyroid cancer that allows for removal of cancerous tissue while preserving some thyroid function."|&lt;SEP&gt;Lobectomy may be used in certain cases of thyroid cancer management, allowing for less extensive surgery while still addressing the disease."|</data>
      <data key="d6">surgery, cancer treatment&lt;SEP&gt;surgical treatment, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;surgical treatment, disease management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Papillary Thyroid Carcinoma (PTC)">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Papillary thyroid carcinoma represents the most common form of thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">classification, cancer type</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Completion Thyroidectomy">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Completion thyroidectomy is performed as a treatment option when the original surgery shows high-risk features for thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical treatment, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="NIFTP">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NIFTP is classified as a type of thyroid cancer that is noninvasive and does not require further treatment beyond surgical removal.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer classification, treatment pathway</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="RAI Therapy">
      <data key="d4">26.0</data>
      <data key="d5">RAI therapy is commonly recommended after thyroidectomy to target and destroy any lingering cancer cells."|&lt;SEP&gt;RAI therapy is commonly used for targeting thyroid cancer cells following surgery to minimize recurrence risks."|&lt;SEP&gt;RAI therapy may be implemented after total thyroidectomy for patients diagnosed with aggressive thyroid cancer types to eliminate remaining cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-operative treatment, cancer therapy&lt;SEP&gt;post-surgical treatment, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;therapeutic intervention, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Lenvatinib">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lenvatinib is employed in cases of advanced thyroid cancer where traditional surgical treatments are ineffective."|&lt;SEP&gt;Lenvatinib is utilized as a targeted treatment for aggressive thyroid cancer cases that cannot be removed via surgery."|</data>
      <data key="d6">targeted therapy, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;targeted therapy, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Sorafenib">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Sorafenib is a treatment option for advanced thyroid cancer, particularly for patients exhibiting specific genetic mutations."|&lt;SEP&gt;Sorafenib serves as a treatment option for advanced thyroid cancer, especially in patients who have undergone other treatments."|</data>
      <data key="d6">targeted therapy, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;targeted therapy, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Cabozantinib">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Cabozantinib is recommended for the management of progressing thyroid cancer after initial treatment options have failed."|&lt;SEP&gt;Cabozantinib is used to manage progressive thyroid cancer after other treatment avenues have been explored."|</data>
      <data key="d6">targeted therapy, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;targeted therapy, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="CT Scan">
      <data key="d4">14.0</data>
      <data key="d5">CT scans are used to monitor the progression or recurrence of thyroid cancer by providing detailed internal images."|&lt;SEP&gt;CT scans are utilized for assessing potential metastasis of thyroid cancer, enhancing monitoring efficacy."|</data>
      <data key="d6">imaging procedure, cancer monitoring&lt;SEP&gt;imaging technique, cancer assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="MRI">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">MRIs may be employed to assess soft tissue changes in thyroid cancer patients, aiding in monitoring for recurrence or metastasis."|</data>
      <data key="d6">imaging procedure, cancer monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Cancer" target="Follow-Up Care">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Follow-up care is essential in monitoring thyroid cancer patients after treatment to check for recurrence and manage long-term health."|</data>
      <data key="d6">post-treatment management, surveillance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Gland" target="Thyroid Hormones">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The thyroid gland is responsible for producing thyroid hormones essential for regulating metabolism and overall health.</data>
      <data key="d6">endocrine function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Gland" target="Parathyroid Glands">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The parathyroid glands are situated near the thyroid and play a crucial role in calcium regulation in conjunction with thyroid function.</data>
      <data key="d6">glandular relationship</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Gland" target="TSH">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Thyroid Gland's function is influenced by TSH, which regulates hormone production to maintain metabolic homeostasis.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormonal regulation, endocrine function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Gland" target="Hyperthyroidism">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hyperthyroidism results from overactivity of the Thyroid Gland, leading to excessive hormone production.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease state, glandular function</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Gland" target="Radioactive Iodine (RAI) Uptake Test">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The RAI Uptake Test evaluates the function of the Thyroid Gland by assessing iodine uptake, crucial for diagnosing thyroid disorders.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic tool, thyroid evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid Nodules" target="Symptoms of Thyroid Nodules">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thyroid nodules can present symptoms that affect quality of life, indicating their potential to lead to more serious health issues.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical symptoms</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Older Persons" target="Bone Marrow Involvement">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Older persons are more likely to experience bone marrow involvement in diseases, increasing health risks as age progresses.</data>
      <data key="d6">age-related health risks</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DLBCL" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">DLBCL is predominantly treated with chemotherapy as a primary intervention strategy to manage the aggressive nature of the lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DLBCL" target="ISRT">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">ISRT may be used in localized DLBCL cases to target sites directly affected by lymphoma, indicating treatment precision.</data>
      <data key="d6">targeted therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoimmunotherapy" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoimmunotherapy combines chemotherapy with immunotherapy to provide a more robust treatment approach for lymphomas.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment strategy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nodules" target="Thyroid Hormone">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Nodules assessed for hormone production are crucial for determining malignancy risk and classification of thyroid conditions.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnosis, hormone production</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nodules" target="Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biopsy is performed on suspicious nodules to determine the presence of cancerous cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, cancer testing</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Medullary Thyroid Cancer" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgery is often indicated for treating medullary thyroid cancer to ensure removal of affected tissue.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment, surgical intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Anaplastic Thyroid Cancer" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">If diagnosed with anaplastic thyroid cancer, surgery may be required despite its aggressive nature.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment, surgical necessity</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lobectomy" target="Thyroid Hormone Replacement Therapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Following a lobectomy, some patients may require thyroid hormone replacement to support metabolic function.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-surgery management, treatment necessity</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lobectomy" target="Total Thyroidectomy">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Lobectomy may be a preliminary step, but if cancer is found to be invasive, total thyroidectomy is likely performed.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical procedure, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Thyroid Hormone Replacement Therapy">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A total thyroidectomy necessitates lifelong thyroid hormone replacement to manage hormonal levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Patients who undergo total thyroidectomy will require thyroid hormone replacement therapy to compensate for hormone loss.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-operative care, hormone management&lt;SEP&gt;treatment, post-operative care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Total Thyroidectomy is a surgical option for aggressive forms of thyroid cancer, often requiring extensive management post-procedure.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical intervention, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Follicular Thyroid Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Total thyroidectomy is recommended for patients diagnosed with follicular thyroid carcinoma that has grown beyond the thyroid.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical treatment, cancer intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Oncocytic Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Total thyroidectomy is also necessary when oncocytic carcinoma is determined to have invaded surrounding tissues.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical treatment, cancer intervention</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="RAI Therapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">RAI therapy may be recommended after total thyroidectomy if there is a risk of residual cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-surgery treatment, cancer therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Neck Ultrasound">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Neck ultrasounds are routinely recommended after total thyroidectomy to monitor for any signs of cancer recurrence."|</data>
      <data key="d6">monitoring, disease surveillance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Blood Tests">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood tests following total thyroidectomy are crucial for tracking hormone levels and ensuring no recurrence of thyroid cancer."|</data>
      <data key="d6">monitoring, health assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Levothyroxine" target="Thyroid">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Levothyroxine may be prescribed to patients following thyroid surgery to help regulate hormone levels after removal of the thyroid tissue.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormone treatment, post-operative care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Levothyroxine" target="Completion Thyroidectomy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Following a completion thyroidectomy, Levothyroxine is often required to ensure hormone levels remain stable, depending on the extent of the surgery.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormone therapy, treatment post-surgery</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hyperthyroidism" target="Thyroid Hormone Levels">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Elevated Thyroid Hormone Levels are indicative of Hyperthyroidism, necessitating further evaluation and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnosis indicator, hormonal imbalance</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pathology Report" target="Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A Pathology Report is generated following a Biopsy to provide crucial information regarding the presence and type of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnosis documentation, cancer confirmation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Differentiated Thyroid Cancer" target="Surgery">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Surgical treatments are often prescribed for Differentiated Thyroid Cancer, making it essential for patient management.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment approach, cancer type</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyrotropin Alfa (Thyrogen)" target="RAI">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thyrogen is used to increase TSH levels in patients prior to RAI therapy, enhancing its effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormonal therapy, treatment preparation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
    </edge>
