    <edge source="Biopsy" target="Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d4">54.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A Biopsy is used to diagnose Prostate Cancer by analyzing tissue samples from the prostate.&lt;SEP&gt;A biopsy is a critical procedure for confirming the presence of prostate cancer through sampled tissue analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A biopsy is a critical procedure to diagnose prostate cancer by obtaining tissue samples for analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A biopsy is essential for confirming the diagnosis of prostate cancer after initial tests suggest its presence.&lt;SEP&gt;A biopsy is necessary to confirm the diagnosis of prostate cancer after potential identification through testing.</data>
