    <edge source="CT Scan" target="MRI">
      <data key="d4">32.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Both CT and MRI are medical imaging techniques used to visualize internal structures for diagnostic purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Both MRI and CT scans are advanced imaging techniques used to visualize internal organs and tissues, particularly in the context of cancer diagnosis and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;When MRI is unavailable, a CT scan serves as an alternative imaging method to assist in the diagnosis of primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic alternatives, imaging technology&lt;SEP&gt;imaging technology, cancer diagnostics&lt;SEP&gt;medical imaging, diagnostics</data>
