      <data key="d4">51.0</data>
      <data key="d5">CT scans are a common type of imaging test used to diagnose and monitor cancer patients.&lt;SEP&gt;CT scans are a specific type of imaging test used to generate detailed images of body structures, crucial for cancer assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;CT scans are a subtype of imaging tests used to diagnose internal injuries and conditions, including cancer-related issues.&lt;SEP&gt;CT scans are a type of imaging test frequently used for evaluating cancer progression and assessing treatment response.&lt;SEP&gt;CT scans are a type of imaging test used to visualize internal structures and detect abnormalities in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;CT scans are one type of imaging test used to identify any spread of leukemia beyond the bone marrow.</data>
